WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:00.400
All right.

00:00.400 --> 00:03.840
So now I hope that you have downloaded all the tools and created the accounts.

00:03.880 --> 00:06.400
Now it's time to move to a very important step.

00:06.400 --> 00:12.680
That's almost all people skip while doing projects, and that is by creating the project plan.

00:12.680 --> 00:15.120
And for that we will be using the tool notion.

00:15.160 --> 00:21.200
Notion is of course a free tool, and it can help you to organize your ideas, your plans and resources

00:21.360 --> 00:22.400
all in one place.

00:22.400 --> 00:27.000
I use it very intensively for my private projects, like for example, creating this course.

00:27.000 --> 00:30.520
And I can tell you creating a project plan is the key to success.

00:30.520 --> 00:36.200
Creating a data warehouse project is usually very complex, and according to Gartner reports, over

00:36.200 --> 00:39.080
50% of data warehouse projects fail.

00:39.120 --> 00:41.320
And my opinion about any complex projects.

00:41.520 --> 00:45.040
The key to success is to have a clear project plan.

00:45.080 --> 00:50.080
So now at this phase of the project, we're going to go and create a rough project plan, because at

00:50.080 --> 00:54.080
the moment we don't have yet clear understanding about the data architecture.

00:54.080 --> 00:54.760
So let's go.

00:54.800 --> 00:54.960
Okay.

00:55.000 --> 00:58.320
So now let's create a new page and let's call it data warehouse projects.

00:58.320 --> 01:03.840
The first thing that we have to go and create the main phases and stages of the projects.

01:03.840 --> 01:05.080
And for that we need a table.

01:05.080 --> 01:11.760
So in order to do that, hit slash and then type database inline and then let's go and call it something

01:11.760 --> 01:13.920
like Data Warehouse Epics.

01:13.920 --> 01:16.680
And we're going to go and hide it because I don't like it.

01:16.680 --> 01:22.680
And then on the table we can go and rename it like for example projects, epics, something like that.

01:22.720 --> 01:26.360
And now what we're going to do, we're going to go and list all the big tasks of the projects.

01:26.360 --> 01:30.920
So an epic is usually like a large task that needs a lot of efforts in order to solve it.

01:30.920 --> 01:35.080
So you can call it epics, stages, phases of the project, whatever you want.

01:35.120 --> 01:37.520
So we're going to go and list our project steps.

01:37.520 --> 01:44.000
So let's start with the requirements analysis and then designing data architecture.

01:44.720 --> 01:49.600
And another one we have the projects initialization.

01:49.600 --> 01:52.360
So those are the three big tasks in the project first.

01:52.400 --> 01:53.320
And now what do we need.

01:53.320 --> 01:57.480
We need another table for the small chunks of the tasks the subtasks.

01:57.480 --> 01:58.600
And we're going to do the same thing.

01:58.600 --> 01:59.920
So we're going to go and hit slash.

01:59.920 --> 02:02.320
And we're going to search for the table inline.

02:02.320 --> 02:03.560
And we're going to do the same thing.

02:03.560 --> 02:06.480
So first we're going to call it data warehouse tasks.

02:06.480 --> 02:08.440
And then we're going to hide it.

02:08.440 --> 02:12.950
And over here we're going to rename it I say this is the project tasks.

02:12.950 --> 02:13.870
So now what we're going to do.

02:13.870 --> 02:17.950
We're going to go to the plus icon over here and then search for relation.

02:17.950 --> 02:19.430
This one over here with the arrow.

02:19.470 --> 02:22.790
And now we're going to search for the name of the first table.

02:22.790 --> 02:25.150
So we called it Data Warehouse Epics.

02:25.150 --> 02:26.430
So let's go and click it.

02:26.430 --> 02:28.910
And we're going to say as well two way relation.

02:28.910 --> 02:31.230
So let's go and add the relation.

02:31.230 --> 02:34.990
So with that we got a filled in the new table called Data Warehouse Epics.

02:35.030 --> 02:36.470
This comes from this table.

02:36.470 --> 02:40.710
And as well we have here data warehouse tasks that comes from the below table.

02:40.710 --> 02:42.470
So as you can see we have linked them together.

02:42.470 --> 02:45.190
Now what I'm going to do I'm going to take this to the left side.

02:45.190 --> 02:49.270
And then what we're going to do, we're going to go and select one of those epics like for example,

02:49.270 --> 02:51.710
let's take design the data architecture.

02:51.710 --> 02:56.390
And now what we're going to do, we're going to go and break down this epic into multiple tasks like

02:56.390 --> 03:00.190
for example, choose data management approach.

03:00.830 --> 03:02.510
And then we have another task what we're going to do.

03:02.510 --> 03:05.190
We're going to go and select as well the same epic.

03:05.190 --> 03:09.790
So maybe the next step is brainstorm and design the layers.

03:10.510 --> 03:14.550
And then let's go to another epic, for example the project initialization.

03:14.550 --> 03:19.790
And we say over here, for example, create git repo, prepare the structure.

03:20.470 --> 03:23.230
We can go and make another one in the same epic.

03:23.270 --> 03:27.150
Let's say we're going to go and create the database and the schemas.

03:27.150 --> 03:30.910
So as you can see I'm just defining the subtasks of those epics.

03:30.910 --> 03:31.670
So now what we're going to do.

03:31.670 --> 03:35.990
We're going to go and add a checkbox in order to understand whether we have done the task or not.

03:35.990 --> 03:38.910
So we go to the plus and search for check.

03:38.910 --> 03:40.230
We need the checkbox.

03:40.230 --> 03:41.070
And what we're going to do.

03:41.070 --> 03:44.270
We're going to make it really small like this.

03:44.270 --> 03:48.190
And with that, each time we are done with the task, we're going to go and click on it just to make

03:48.230 --> 03:49.830
sure that we have done the task.

03:49.830 --> 03:53.550
Now there is one more thing that is not really working nice and that is here.

03:53.550 --> 03:57.070
We're going to have like a long list of tasks and it's really annoying.

03:57.070 --> 04:01.070
So what we're going to do, we're going to go to the plus over here and let's search for rollup.

04:01.230 --> 04:02.390
So let's go and select it.

04:02.390 --> 04:03.230
So now what we're going to do.

04:03.230 --> 04:05.110
We have to go and select the relationship.

04:05.110 --> 04:06.910
It's going to be the data warehouse task.

04:06.910 --> 04:10.310
And after that we're going to go to the property and make it as a checkbox.

04:10.310 --> 04:14.510
So now as you can see in the first table we are saying how many tasks is closed.

04:14.510 --> 04:15.910
But I don't want to show it like this.

04:15.910 --> 04:20.780
What you can do, we're going to go to the calculation and to the percent and then percent checked.

04:20.780 --> 04:23.740
And with that we can see the progress of our projects.

04:23.740 --> 04:26.580
And now instead of the numbers, we can have really nice bar.

04:26.620 --> 04:27.060
Great.

04:27.060 --> 04:29.780
So as will we can go and give it a name like progress.

04:29.780 --> 04:30.940
So that's it.

04:30.940 --> 04:33.420
And we can go and hide the data warehouse tasks.

04:33.460 --> 04:36.500
And now with that we have really nice progress bar for each epic.

04:36.500 --> 04:41.020
And if you close all the tasks of this epic, we can see that we have reached 100%.

04:41.020 --> 04:42.260
So this is the main structure.

04:42.260 --> 04:47.300
Now we can go and add some cosmetics and rename stuff in order to make things look nicer.

04:47.340 --> 04:53.540
Like for example, if I go to the tasks over here, I can go and call it tasks and as well go and change

04:53.540 --> 04:55.260
the icon to something like this.

04:55.260 --> 04:59.220
And if you'd like to have an icon for all those epics, what you're going to do, we're going to go

04:59.220 --> 05:01.660
to the epic, for example, design that architecture.

05:01.660 --> 05:06.780
And then if you hover on top of the title, you can see add an icon and you can go and pick any icon

05:06.780 --> 05:08.100
that you want.

05:08.140 --> 05:09.260
So for example this one.

05:09.260 --> 05:11.900
And now as you can see we have defined it here at the top.

05:11.900 --> 05:14.700
And the icon going to be as well in the below table okay.

05:14.740 --> 05:20.260
So now one more thing that we can do for the project tasks is that we can go and group them by the epics.

05:20.260 --> 05:25.780
So if you go to the three dots and then we go to groups and then we can group up by the apex.

05:25.820 --> 05:31.100
As you can see now we have like a section for each epic and you can go and sort the epics if you want.

05:31.140 --> 05:37.300
If you go over here sorts then manual, and you can go over here and start sorting the epics as you

05:37.300 --> 05:37.620
want.

05:37.660 --> 05:40.500
And with that you can expand and minimize each task.

05:40.500 --> 05:43.500
If you don't want to see always all tasks in one go.

05:43.620 --> 05:47.460
So this is a really nice way in order to build like data management for your projects.

05:47.460 --> 05:52.780
Of course, in companies we use professional tools in order to do projects like for example, JIRA,

05:52.780 --> 05:58.060
but for private personal projects that I do, I always do it like this, and I really recommend you

05:58.060 --> 06:02.140
to do it not only for this project, for any project that you are doing, because if you see the whole

06:02.140 --> 06:07.940
project in one go, you can see the big picture and closing tasks and doing it like this, these small

06:07.940 --> 06:13.140
things can makes you really satisfied and keeps you motivated to finish the whole project and makes

06:13.140 --> 06:13.980
you proud.

06:14.020 --> 06:14.620
Okay friends.

06:14.620 --> 06:17.140
So now I just went and added few icons.

06:17.180 --> 06:20.420
I renamed stuff and as well more tasks for each epic.

06:20.460 --> 06:22.980
And this is gonna be our starting point in the project.

06:22.980 --> 06:27.980
And once we have more informations, we're going to go and add more details on how exactly we're going

06:28.020 --> 06:29.420
to build the data warehouse.

06:29.420 --> 06:32.850
So at the start, we're going to go and analyze and understand the requirements.

06:32.850 --> 06:37.050
And only after that we're going to start designing the data architecture.

06:37.050 --> 06:38.690
And here we have three tasks.

06:38.850 --> 06:41.250
First we have to choose the data management approach.

06:41.250 --> 06:46.530
And after that we're going to do brainstorming and designing the layers of the data warehouse.

06:46.530 --> 06:49.730
And at the end we're going to go and draw a data architecture.

06:49.730 --> 06:53.850
So with that we have clear understanding how the data architecture looks like.

06:53.890 --> 06:58.210
And after that we're going to go to the next topic where we're going to start preparing our projects.

06:58.210 --> 07:03.330
So once we have a clear understanding of the data architecture, the first task here is to go and create

07:03.370 --> 07:05.090
detailed project tasks.

07:05.090 --> 07:07.730
So we're going to go and add more epics and more tasks.

07:07.730 --> 07:12.330
And once we are done, then we're going to go and create the naming conventions for the projects just

07:12.330 --> 07:15.530
to make sure that we have rules and standards in the whole project.

07:15.530 --> 07:19.970
And next we're going to go and create a repository in the git, and we're going to prepare as well the

07:19.970 --> 07:23.810
structure of the repository, so that we always commit our work there.

07:23.810 --> 07:28.290
And then we can start with the first script where we can create a database and schemas.

07:28.290 --> 07:31.490
So my friends this is the initial plan for the projects.

07:31.530 --> 07:33.410
Now let's start with the first epic.

07:33.450 --> 07:35.450
We have the requirements analysis.
